id: constraint.loop_safety
category: constraint
status: verified
date: 2026-08-24
content: 'Hard limits prevent infinite loops: max_turns=25, max_tokens_total=131072,
  max_wall_time=600s, repetition_threshold=3.'
notes: 'LoopSafetyMonitor tracks: tool repetition, token usage, wall time, turn count

  Warning at 5 repeated tools, block at 8

  Window size: 20 turns (increased from 10 to reduce false positives)

  Pattern 4 (same-tool-name-3x) removed — replaced with arg-aware logic

  These limits are non-negotiable — they protect the system from runaway execution

  '
metadata: {}
prerequisites: []
blocking: []
tags:
- loop-safety
- hard-limits
- guardrails
- reliability
---
id: constraint.never_delete_user_files
category: constraint
status: verified
date: 2026-08-24
content: NEVER delete user files, games, or applications without explicit user confirmation.
  Steam apps are especially protected.
notes: 'File deletion is a destructive operation — always verify before executing

  Steam apps/games are never to be removed under any circumstances

  User data is sacred — the system should never assume it can safely delete

  When in doubt, ask the user rather than risk data loss

  This is a hard constraint, not a preference

  '
metadata: {}
prerequisites: []
blocking: []
tags:
- safety
- user-data
- deletion
- steam
- protection
---
id: constraint.no_secret_logging
category: constraint
status: verified
date: ''
content: API keys, tokens, passwords, and credentials are never logged, printed, or
  stored in plain text. They are read from environment variables or secret managers.
notes: ''
